ion 1 with the corresponding letter numbering>\",\n\"answer_q2\": \"<Respond to the Question 2 with the corresponding letter numbering>\"\n\n    }\n``` \n    \n\n## Scenario\nSasha recently moved to Mexico for work and had to learn Spanish quickly. She took some lessons and thought she was doing okay in her new language. At a departmental lunch, she tried to compliment her coworker's outfit but ended up saying \"You look like a chicken\" without realizing it due to a mix-up in her vocabulary.\n\n## Question 1\nWhat emotion(s) would Sasha's coworker ultimately feel in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 1\nA) Disapproval\nB) Embarrassment\nC) Jealousy\nD) Gratitude\nE) Caring\nF) Guilt\n\n## Question 2\nWhy would Sasha's coworker feel these emotions in this situation?\n\n## Choices for Question 2\nA) Sasha is trying to learn Spanish\nB) Sasha criticized her outfit\nC) Sasha complimented her outfit\nD) Sasha disrespected her Spanish proficiency","options":null,"imageContent":null,"audioContent":null,"videoContent":null,"reminderContext":null,"videoCoverUrl":null,"chips":null,"customMessage":null,"media":null,"mediaTime":null,"interceptContent":null,"contents":[],"imgs":null,"regenerations":0,"seqNum":2,"responseSource":"agent:llm","isSuicide":false,"isSuicideConf":0.006690882588680618,"emotions":[],"relationId":"6af3e8f8d6006945d280af41","courseProgressId":0,"tsGen":1794369784318,"createTime":"2026-11-11 12:03:04","delFlag":0,"emotionTendency":null,"sourceProductType":null,"sourceProductId":null,"consultantBotId":null,"consultantUserId":null}],"first":true,"last":true},"nonce":"cd608032cf164fa79d64403ebf6ae881"}